{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"RCA/design escalation (2026-08-17), before reproduction or code edits. The missing project-region premise is confirmed, but the proposed value is contradicted by current repository authorities: .github/llm-providers/bedrock.toml records successful invocation in account 896586841071 / us-east-1; external-integration.yml defaults both AWS_DEFAULT_REGION and REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_REGION to us-east-1; infra/runbooks/bedrock-access.md directs the bot service to us-east-1; compose defaults likewise use us-east-1. The ticket proposal instead names us-west-2 solely from the local frontier-bedrock profile. Pinning that silently would change the project-wide Bedrock endpoint away from the measured CI/service default.\n\nA second contract issue is proven statically: LLMConfig.from_env resolves CLI/env/file into one bedrock_region_name string, discarding origin. resolve_bedrock_region currently labels every configured non-empty value as REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_REGION, so a rebar.toml pin cannot truthfully satisfy the ticket AC requiring provider provenance region_source=repo-config without adding source metadata/plumbing.\n\nDecision required. Recommended: pin us-east-1 in rebar.toml, matching measured CI/service authority, and include truthful config-source provenance plumbing in this bug; retain REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_REGION override precedence. Alternatives: pin us-west-2 as the new project default based on the local profile, or leave project config unpinned and classify fresh-shell setup as an operator-profile/env issue. No production edit or gate reproduction has started pending the decision."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787027314462699001,"uuid":"164ce339-6ce8-426e-9d04-8b7256b2a0ea"}